Darwin: Alright... explain it quickly.
Logos: In this world, enemies attack using statements. Your task is to determine what those statements mean.
Darwin: So I fight by answering questions?
Logos: Correct. If your answer is correct, you deal damage. If you are wrong, you lose Mental Stability.
Logos: You only need a few symbols to begin.
Logos: The symbol ¬ means NOT, and it flips the truth of a statement.
Logos: The symbol ∧ means AND, which requires both parts to be true.
Logos: The symbol ∨ means OR, which is true if at least one part is true.
Darwin: ...That's it?
Logos: For now. You will learn the rest as you progress.
Logos: The first floor will test how well you understand truth itself. 

#Evaluation
Logos: Answer these before you proceed.

~ question_1
Logos: First: What does ¬P mean?
- A. It means P is always true.
	Logos: No. You are reversing meaning incorrectly. ¬ always flips truth.
	=> question_1

- B. It means P is false (NOT P)
	Logos: Correct. ¬ negates the statement entirely.
	~ question_2
	Logos: Second: If P is true, what happens to ¬P?
	- A. It becomes true
		Logos: No. You are ignoring inversion.
		=> question_2

	- B. It becomes undefined
		Logos: No. You are ignoring inversion.
		=> question_2

	- C. It becomes false
		Logos: Correct. Negation flips truth.
		~ question_3
		Logos: Third: When is P ∧ Q true?
		- A. When at least one is true
			Logos: No. AND requires full agreement.
			=> question_3

		- B. When both are true
			Logos: Correct. Both conditions must hold.
			~ question_4
			Logos: Fourth: When is P ∨ Q false?
			- A. When both are true
				Logos: No. OR only collapses when both sides fail.
				=> question_4

			- B. When both are false 
				Logos: Correct. OR fails only when nothing is true.
				Logos: You may now proceed.
				=> END

			- C. When one is true
				Logos: No. OR only collapses when both sides fail.
				=> question_4

			- D. Never false
				Logos: No. OR only collapses when both sides fail.
				=> question_4

		- C. When both are false
			Logos: No. AND requires full agreement.
			=> question_3

		- D. When P is false only
			Logos: No. AND requires full agreement.
			=> question_3

	- D. It becomes both true and false
		Logos: No. You are ignoring inversion.
		=> question_2

- C. It means P and Q are both true
	Logos: No. You are reversing meaning incorrectly. ¬ always flips truth.
	=> question_1

- D. It means P or Q is true
	Logos: No. You are reversing meaning incorrectly. ¬ always flips truth.
	=> question_1
=> END